messages:
Ava (Docs): FYI I pushed a compact doc that combines troubleshooting for 429s, timeouts, and context trimming with a small SDK snippet section. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4199. Looking for quick sign-offs on accuracy and one small phrasing nit (see below).

Raj (Eng): Skimmed it. Mostly good. One factual nit: our runtime will not do cross-region fallback if customer has `restrict_cross_region: true`. Might be worth an explicit callout + example config snippet.

Ava (Docs): Good catch. I'll add a callout block: "Cross-region fallbacks are only attempted when cross-region routing is enabled." Want sample JSON config text?

Raj (Eng): Yes — something like `{ "routing": { "allow_cross_region": false } }` is fine. Also, for timeouts: we should recommend a client-side overall request timeout (e.g., 30s) and a smaller per-try timeout so retries don't extend infinitely.

Eli (SDK): Adding the JS + Python snippets now. My plan: show a minimal `retryOn429` helper that checks `err.headers['retry-after']` then does exponential backoff with jitter if absent. Also show `trimConversation(history, maxTokens)` helper that returns the most recent messages until token cap.

Ava (Docs): Example wording I want to add: "If the service returns 429, prefer honoring Retry-After when present. When it's absent, use exponential backoff (base 200ms, max 10s) with jitter and limit total retries to 3 by default." Is that aligned with SDK defaults?

Eli (SDK): Yes — SDK default is 3 retries for idempotent-ish generate calls, base backoff 200ms, multiplier 2, jitter 0.25, max 10s. Will add a code snippet.

Harper (PM): Tiny ask: add one short sentence about canary rollouts possibly showing spikes in 429s and to consider temporarily reducing traffic % if p99 exceeds target. Nothing heavy, just ops guidance.

Ava (Docs): Will do. Also, LinkBot flagged an older reference to `/docs/retries` as deprecated. I removed it and replaced with the new consolidated guide.

Eli (SDK): Pasting the JS pseudo-snippet I'll include in PR: `// retryOn429 helper
async function requestWith429Handling(client, payload){
  for(let attempt=0; attempt<3; attempt++){
    try{
      return await client.generate(payload);
    }catch(err){
      if(err.status !== 429) throw err;
      const ra = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after'] || '0',10);
      if(ra>0) await sleep(ra*1000);
      else await sleep(Math.min(10000, 200 * Math.pow(2, attempt)) * (1 + (Math.random()-0.5)*0.5));
    }
  }
  throw new Error('exhausted retries');
}`

Eli (SDK): Also adding `trimConversation` pseudo-code: `function trimConversation(messages, maxTokens=2048){ /* keep last messages until tokenCount<=maxTokens */ }`

Raj (Eng): +1. Can you add a tiny `curl` example showing `Retry-After` in headers? Ops likes that.

Eli (SDK): Will do: `curl -i -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -d '{"model":"redwood-1.0","input":"..."}' https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate` and mention server may respond `Retry-After: 5`.

Ava (Docs): Plan: add the config callout, canary note, and the three snippets (JS, Python, curl), then ship after 24-36h if no objections. Tagging @Raj and @Eli for final quick review. :thumbsup:

LinkBot: Note: replaced deprecated link `/docs/retries` with `/docs/troubleshooting/fallbacks` in 3 files.

Ava (Docs): Thanks all — I'll update PR now and drop a final comment when ready for merge.
